T* (       Not Indicated: Radiation therapy is generally not a primary treatment modality for advanced epithelial ovarian) Tj
T* (cancer \(EOC\) like Stage IIIC HGSOC. The disease is typically widespread within the peritoneal cavity \(T3c\) and) Tj
T* (involves lymph nodes \(N1\), making it unsuitable for local or regional radiation with curative intent.) Tj
T* (       Historical Context: Whole Abdominal Radiation Therapy \(WART\) was explored historically but has largely been) Tj
T* (abandoned due to significant toxicity \(e.g., renal, gastrointestinal, hepatic\) and the advent of highly effective) Tj
T* (systemic chemotherapy.) Tj
T* (       Current Guidelines: NCCN and ESMO guidelines for advanced EOC focus on surgery \(PDS or NACT-IDS\)) Tj
T* (followed by platinum-based chemotherapy and appropriate maintenance therapy \(PARP inhibitors or bevacizumab\),) Tj
T* (especially in BRCA-mutated/HRD-positive cases like this. Radiation is not listed as a primary or adjuvant) Tj
T* (consolidative treatment.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.  Adjuvant/Consolidative Role:) Tj
T* (       There is no evidence to support the routine use of consolidative or adjuvant radiation therapy after optimal) Tj
T* (cytoreduction and systemic chemotherapy in this setting. The focus remains on systemic control and maintenance.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.  Potential Future Role \(Palliative\):) Tj
T* (       Radiation therapy may be considered in the recurrent setting for palliation of localized symptomatic disease.) Tj
T* (This could include:) Tj
T* (           Localized painful bone metastases.) Tj
T* (           Symptomatic brain metastases.) Tj
T* (           Localized pelvic or abdominal masses causing pain, bleeding, or obstruction, where systemic therapy alone is) Tj
